# Obsidian keeps two kinds of state in .obsidian/. The shared settings —
# which folders to ignore, and the decision to write markdown links rather
# than wikilinks so the docs still render on GitHub — belong to the project
# and are committed. Which panes happen to be open on one machine does not.
.obsidian/workspace.json
.obsidian/workspace-mobile.json
.obsidian/cache
.obsidian/graph.json

# Machine-specific notes for Claude Code — JDK path, this laptop's LAN IP, which
# GitHub account the remote uses. Facts about whoever is testing, not about the
# app, for the same reason 0490a9d took the server address out of the source tree.
CLAUDE.local.md
